Student Performance Analysis System
Data Science Mini Project — NumPy + Pandas + Matplotlib

NumPy Pandas Matplotlib EDA Data Visualization
Project description 
This project builds a complete Student Performance Analysis System using Python's three core data science libraries — NumPy, Pandas, and Matplotlib. The system reads a dataset of students (name, marks in 5 subjects, attendance percentage, and study hours), performs statistical analysis, assigns grades, and generates a rich visual report with multiple charts.

The project covers the full data science workflow: data generation → cleaning → computation → visualization → insight reporting. It demonstrates real-world use of all three libraries working together, making it ideal for a college or university mini-project submission.

Project Modules
Module 1 — Data Generation (NumPy)
Generate a random dataset of 50 students containing names, subject marks, attendance percentage, and daily study hours using NumPy's random functions.

Module 2 — Data Processing (Pandas)
Load the data into a Pandas DataFrame, calculate total and average marks for each student, assign letter grades (A/B/C/D/F) based on score ranges, and determine pass/fail status.

Module 3 — Statistical Analysis (NumPy + Pandas)
Compute key statistics including mean, median, and standard deviation of marks. Identify the top-performing and lowest-performing students, and calculate subject-wise class averages.

Module 4 — Visualization (Matplotlib)
Create a 6-chart dashboard in a single figure — a bar chart for subject averages, a pie chart for grade distribution, a histogram for marks spread, a scatter plot for study hours vs marks, a correlation heatmap, and a horizontal bar chart for the top 10 students.

Module 5 — Report & CSV Export
Print a formatted summary report to the console showing class statistics, grade breakdown, and top 5 students. Export the fully processed and ranked student data to a CSV file for record-keeping.
