Project Title:
Retail Sales Performance Analysis & Dashboard
(Using NumPy, Pandas, and Matplotlib)

Project Objective
Analyze 4 years of retail sales data for a superstore to discover key business insights, trends, and patterns. Create professional visualizations and generate actionable recommendations for business improvement.

What You Need to Do in This Project
1. Data Loading & Cleaning

Load the dataset using Pandas
Handle missing values
Remove duplicate rows
Convert date columns to proper datetime format
Create new derived columns:
Year, Month, Quarter
Profit Margin
Sales Category (High/Medium/Low)
Any other useful features using NumPy and Pandas


2. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)

Calculate total sales, profit, quantity, and average order value
Compute Year-over-Year (YoY) and Month-over-Month (MoM) growth
Find top 10 and bottom 10 products by sales and profit
Analyze performance by:
Region
State
Category & Sub-Category
Customer Segment (Consumer, Corporate, Home Office)
Shipping Mode


3. Advanced Analysis

Identify sales seasonality and peak periods
Analyze the relationship between Discount and Profit
Correlation analysis between numerical variables (using NumPy)
Profitability analysis by customer segment and product category
Detect loss-making products and regions
Outlier detection in sales and profit

4. Data Visualization (Using Matplotlib)
Create the following charts:

Line plots: Monthly and yearly sales & profit trends
Bar charts: Top 10 products, top regions, category-wise sales
Horizontal bar charts: Bottom performing products
Pie / Donut charts: Sales contribution by segment and category
Heatmap: Correlation matrix
Box plots: Distribution of sales and profit
Subplots: Multiple charts in one figure for comparison
Histogram: Discount distribution

5. Insights & Business Recommendations

Summarize key findings
Provide clear, actionable recommendations based on the analysis (e.g., which categories need attention, best time for promotions, etc.)


Deliverables

Jupyter Notebook (.ipynb) with clean, well-commented code
All visualizations saved as high-quality images
Final insights and recommendations section at the end

